⭐ CONFIRMED, and the code says so out loud. The SEEKING branch of `applyGathererTick` re-picks ONLY when the current target has gone invalid:
    const current = g.targetSparkId !== null ? world.freeSparks.get(g.targetSparkId) : undefined;
    if (current === undefined || !isHarvestable(current)) g.targetSparkId = pickGathererTarget(world, g);
and `pickGathererTarget`'s own docblock (gathererLifecycle.ts:308-310) states it: *"pickGathererTarget is only called when the current target has become invalid, so mid-walk thrash was already bounded."* That bounded thrash IS the owner's complaint: a unit already walking to a nearest-of-any-type shape will never notice that its QUEUED type has just spawned.
